<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RSW_Zakkro.xml                                  EXTREME_DESERT_CAVERN_BEAST_1

  Authors deep_desert.md SS8's headline cavern creature: "Serious authoring
  effort belongs here — reference the Mandalorian cave-beast: a huge shaggy
  thing deep in a cavern, with massive eggs a Jawa would cross a desert for."
  Cavern map-generation itself is separate, larger work and is explicitly out
  of scope for this item (deep_desert.md's own "Owed" section).

  Canon check (rimworld-canon-references convention): "the Mandalorian
  cave-beast" is Wookieepedia's mudhorn (Arvala-7, *The Mandalorian* Ch. 2 —
  Din Djarin fights one in its cave for its egg). It is ALREADY ported into
  this mod as RSW_Mudhorn (MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1, ThingDefs_Races/
  RSW_Mudhorn.xml) — but as ordinary AridShrubland/Desert ambient wildlife
  (wildBiomes ExtremeDesert 0.0, i.e. explicitly EXCLUDED from this biome),
  tameable, pack-animal, common (combatPower 475), with a plain hatching/food
  egg pair. That def does not serve this design beat: a rare, dangerous,
  cavern-exclusive headline encounter whose egg is a water-canteen, not food.
  Rather than duplicate or repurpose the shipped Mudhorn, this file authors a
  distinct invented species (RSW_Zakkro — coined per check_pseudo_sw_name.py,
  PASS, no collision with any of the 137 canon_references entries) that fills
  the narrative role the sheet actually asks for, and keeps the canon mudhorn
  untouched.

  Recognizability rule: a plain shaggy quadruped predator would read as
  "that's a bear" or "that's a rhino" and fail the strangeness test (this is
  NOT a Star Wars icon, so it gets no icon carve-out). Designed alien instead:
  blind/eyeless, a tendril-fringed lamprey-like sideways maw in place of a
  jaw/horn, matted dust-pale fibrous growths rather than mammal fur. Colour
  and material kept pale/matte/dusty throughout, per the biome's hard ban on
  anything reading mineralized/crystalline/gemstone.

  Body QuadrupedAnimalWithPaws (vanilla, no new BodyDef needed) — claws off
  FrontLeftPaw/FrontRightPaw, bite off Teeth/AnimalJaw, blunt off
  HeadAttackTool, same tool shape as Bear_Grizzly/RSW_Maguana. Sounds reuse
  vanilla Pawn_Bear_* (Call/Angry/Wounded/Death) and the
  Pawn_Melee_BigBash_*/PredatorLarge_Eat set already used elsewhere in this
  mod — no new SoundDefs. leatherDef reuses vanilla Leather_Bear;
  specificMeatDef reuses RSW_Pachydermoid_Meat (already shipped for Mudhorn) —
  no new resource defs beyond the egg this item also asks for (RSW_ZakkroEgg,
  ThingDefs_Items/RSW_ZakkroEgg.xml).

  Deliberately UNWIRED and deliberately no CompProperties_EggLayer:
  - No <wildBiomes> block at all. deep_desert.md SS8 places this creature
    "deep in a cavern", and cavern map-generation does not exist yet (out of
    scope for this item, per its own "Watch out"). Wiring it into a SURFACE
    BiomeDef (ExtremeDesert or otherwise) would be wrong — it has no route to
    appear until cavern generation exists to place it. CAVERNS_PARITY_BUILD_1's
    RSW_Maguana (BiomesTeamPort/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_Maguana.xml) is the
    precedent for shipping a cavern creature def "not wired into any biome by
    this file."
  - No egg-laying comp. deep_desert.md SS4 "Eggs are canteens" is explicit the
    egg is portable water, "not food... drink you can carry" — not a
    hatch/breed mechanic. Wiring CompProperties_EggLayer here would need a
    second (fertilized) egg def this item does not ask for and would turn the
    canteen-egg into ordinary livestock breeding output. Once cavern
    generation exists and a nest-placement/guardian mechanic is designed, a
    later item can decide whether this creature ever lays eggs live in-world;
    today the egg is simply the loot a Jawa takes from its lair.

  Art: checked infrastructure/artpipe/{done,_artsrc,registry.jsonl,
  art_status.json} for "zakkro"/"cave beast"/"cavern beast" first (per
  CLAUDE.md's "Check for existing regenerated art before queuing more") —
  nothing existed. Jobs filed this pass: rsw_zakkro_v1_{south,east,north}
  (living adult, reused across all lifeStages here) and
  rsw_zakkro_dessicated_v1 (desiccated corpse, single non-directional pose,
  same convention as Mudhorn_Dessicated.png). texPaths below are the paths
  the render will land at; validate_patch.py will flag them as pending until
  the artpipe daemon delivers.

  Not wired into MechCluster/ThingSetMaker loot tables or any biome cast —
  that is cavern-generation's job, out of scope here.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RSW_Zakkro</defName>
    <label>zakkro</label>
    <description>A hulking cave-dweller found only deep in the caverns beneath Ash'karr's deep desert, its whole body matted in thick, dust-pale fibrous growths like packed dry lichen — never wet, never shining, powder-pale throughout. It has no eyes: a fringe of short, blunt tendrils rings a wide, sideways-ridged maw where a face would be, reading the cavern by touch and vibration alone. It guards a scattered nest of massive, canteen-heavy eggs somewhere in its territory, and a Jawa clan will cross open sand on the strength of finding one.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.6</MoveSpeed>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-15</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>40</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.2</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <MarketValue>3000</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.97</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>left claw</label>
        <labelNoLocation>claw</labelNoLocation>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>14</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right claw</label>
        <labelNoLocation>claw</labelNoLocation>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>14</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>maw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>24</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.7</chanceFactor>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>haunch</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>20</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
        <chanceFactor>0.3</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPaws</body>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>3.0</maxPreyBodySize>
      <baseHungerRate>1.3</baseHungerRate>
      <baseBodySize>5.5</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>5.5</baseHealthScale>
      <foodType>OmnivoreRoughAnimal, AnimalProduct</foodType>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.9</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>1.0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <nameGenerator>SWAnimalNamerMale</nameGenerator>
      <nameGeneratorFemale>SWAnimalNamerFemale</nameGeneratorFemale>
      <nameOnTameChance>1</nameOnTameChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>60</lifeExpectancy>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <packAnimal>false</packAnimal>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Bear</leatherDef>
      <specificMeatDef>RSW_Pachydermoid_Meat</specificMeatDef>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.3</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.55</minAge>
          <soundCall>Pawn_Bear_Call</soundCall>
          <soundAngry>Pawn_Bear_Angry</soundAngry>
          <soundWounded>Pawn_Bear_Injured</soundWounded>
          <soundDeath>Pawn_Bear_Death</soundDeath>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>PredatorLarge_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
